way for a couple of years now. It's true it took longer to develop the clans outside the original 7, but a lot of that was the problem of reframing them so as not to require the Sabbat to have them make sense. If any clan can belong to any sect, then the Tzimisce can't be Clan Sabbat. Hence the number of drafts of the clan that got returned for revision before they got it right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Utter rejection of humanity is pretty much entirely a Sabbat thing. The Tzimisce in the lore from pre-modern times were not necessarily any less humane than any other clan. Again, the Sabbat's idea of metamorphosis is a perversion of the classic Tzimisce dream of guiding the evolution of both vampire and mortal kind in a novel and productive way (the iconic example being Constantinople). And while alternative philosophies did exist in the medieval period, the Sabbat's hardcore rejection of humanity was as much a reaction against the Convention of Thorns as anything. A great many features of the Sabbat are basically just them defining themselves in opposition to the nascent Camarilla, not because the original Anarch Revolt actually entailed or required any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the Sabbat is not fascist, it was confederate theocratic monarchy currently its a series of terrorist cells/Kratocracy. The Anarch revolt had very little to do with vampire attitudes to humans outside of irritation at elders throwning them under the bus to the 1st inq.<br /> Yes exactly that my point. The Democratic party is fundamentally unsatisfying to socialists like the anarchs are fundamentally unsatisfying to the Tzmisce.<br /> <br /> yes that's how the setting developed as off v5, prior editions it made sense that the tzmisce were mostly Sabbat. Also Ruthven is definitely not illustrious and most lore describes his as Sabbat.<br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lambach_Ruthven\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lambach_Ruthven</a><br /> <br /> that's genrally not true as several clans still gravitate to specific sects with social ramification of that and even if did succeed in what you're proposing it'd be a negative because they've effectively stripped a lot character to achieve to even get it this far.<br /> <br /> Lol no that is explicitly incorrect, pretty much every piece of background lore has said the exact opposite, the dark age tzmisce are genrally relentlessly inhuman its inplicitly and explicitly stated in several books.... I have no idea were you got that idea from, it was such a bold statement you got me second guessing myself so I checked both my two dark age books.<br /> <br /> You've made a lot off odd statements here which contradict the stuff I've read. We're are you getting this from?\u200b Is this some new lore in v5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-10-2023, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}